{"type":"npc","name":"Interstitial Sludge","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":360,"temp":0,"max":360,"details":""},"ac":{"value":30,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":0,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":"spatial hop"},"immunities":[{"type":"cold","exceptions":[]},{"type":"critical-hits","exceptions":[]},{"type":"precision","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]},{"type":"visual","exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"all-damage","value":5,"exceptions":["light","time"],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["khaotan"],"details":"Truespeech"},"level":{"value":15},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Born out of the drippings that seep out of the spaces between planes of existence, interstitial sludges are so dark that they appear almost two-dimensional. These oozes seek gaps in reality where they can slip into the stability of the planes. They resent all creatures that regularly enjoy this stability, lashing out violently against them. When an interstitial sludge would be slain, it is instead drawn back into the void from whence it came.</p><h2>The In-Between</h2><p>Sages deny the existence of a realm between dimensions called the \"In-Between.\" In fact, some grow agitated and even violent when pressed on the issue. The existence of a place outside of all dimensions calls into question reality itself, and suggests that all the known planes are part of a cosmic simulation—a patently absurd notion. Nevertheless, interstitial sludge is from somewhere.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 810/1,850/3,400 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), shield, perception item, skill items (Athletics, Occultism, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, constitution, darkness, elongating, energy resistant (acid, cold, electricity, fire, force, sonic, spirit, vitality, void), fortification, ice, mind, 